# The focus ring waits for the keyboard.
#
# afterhours parks focus on the first focusable widget every frame and paints
# the ring on it regardless of how it got there, so before this rule existed
# the app opened with a blue box around the first view row and every screenshot
# carried it (afterhours_gaps.md #83). The rule: no ring until a navigation key
# is pressed, and none again after a pointer press — the browser's
# :focus-visible heuristic, by hand.
#
# HANABI_FOCUS_AUDIT=1 prints the state next to the version in the sidebar
# footer, read off afterhours' OWN theme.focus_ring_thickness — the number the
# renderer consumes. A build that does not suppress the ring prints "ring on"
# here and fails the first assertion.
#
# settings: {"window_width":1100,"window_height":760,"open_tabs":["t2"],"active_tab":"t2","theme":"dark"}
# env: HANABI_FOCUS_AUDIT=1

# At rest, before anything has been touched: focus is parked on the first row
# and it does NOT wear a ring.
require_thread t2

expect_text "ring off"

# Tab is the user saying they are driving with the keyboard. Now the ring is
# the only thing telling them where they are, so it comes out.
key TAB
wait_frames 6
expect_text "ring on"

# And a click puts it away again: the pointer says where focus is going, so a
# ring left behind is noise.
click_ui sb_new
wait_frames 6
expect_text "ring off"
